adjudication.rationale:
In packages/core/EventManager.ts the diff changes destinationCalendar to an array and adds:

```ts
const [mainHostDestinationCalendar] = evt.destinationCalendar ?? [];
if (evt.location === MeetLocationType && mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration !== "google_calendar") {
  evt["location"] = "integrations:daily";
}
```

If `evt.destinationCalendar` is `undefined`/`null` (or an empty array), destructuring yields `mainHostDestinationCalendar === undefined`. When `evt.location === MeetLocationType` is true, the RHS of `&&` is evaluated and `mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration` throws a TypeError. This is exactly the fallback path (“Google Meet selected w/o a Google Cal”), so the change introduces a real crash that wasn’t present before (previous code used optional chaining).
